invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_vector.c
catches: poly1305_equiv_test
reason: the group loop carries its sums once, not twice, so a word can
  reach 2^33 where the next group's multiply reads 32 bits of it: NEON's
  narrowing move and SSE2's PMULUDQ both drop the rest. The sums stay
  below 2^64, so nothing overflows where a sanitizer would see it; only
  the value is wrong. bin/poly1305_equiv_test compares the accumulator
  with poly1305.c's at every length from 0 to 416 bytes and over 20,000
  random cases.

--- old
    carry_round(once, d);
    carry_round(twice, once);
    h[0] = sums_narrow(twice[0]);
    h[1] = sums_narrow(twice[1]);
    h[2] = sums_narrow(twice[2]);
    h[3] = sums_narrow(twice[3]);
    h[4] = sums_narrow(twice[4]);
--- new
    carry_round(once, d);
    (void)twice;
    h[0] = sums_narrow(once[0]);
    h[1] = sums_narrow(once[1]);
    h[2] = sums_narrow(once[2]);
    h[3] = sums_narrow(once[3]);
    h[4] = sums_narrow(once[4]);
